# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-1 window (the scheduler-side levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-1 (with the branch tp4/agent-turns merged: see ORDER.txt) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix-gate jobs (T0-T3, S1) do not forward the checkpoint (c2_serving_job.MODEL_ACTIONS): they run the base
# weights, which the tier's mechanics (what is spilled, restored and counted) do not depend on.
# L1 (TIMED, the ARM of the first ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-all, the approved ship-4 profile with the gate marker in place of its owner
# waiver id and the four levers on (QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEAN=1, QWEN_PREFIX_HOST_TIER_SPILL_MODE=complete, QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_OWED_CAP_MS=1500,
# QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_SHORT_SHARE=0.65, QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_SHORT_WAIT_S=5, QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_ADAPTIVE=1), the same tests as C1, on Swift. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO
# for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ: c2_smoke_check clean; the lines each lever logs (a lever whose line is absent did
# not engage, and its arm reads NOT_EXERCISED): "[PINDIAG] admission lean split request=... a_ms=... b_ms=... c_ms=... total_ms=..." once per rebound admission, "[PINDIAG]
# admission lean rebind phases request=... fence_ms=... rezero_ms=... project_ms=... copy_ms=... history_ms=... engine_ms=..." once per rebind (where the 188 ms go) and
# "[PINDIAG] admission lean adopt ..." per slot adoption (QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEAN); "[PINDIAG] lever N sched: owed_cap_ms=1500 short_share=0.65 short_wait_s=5" once and
# short=/cap_ms=/guard= on every "lever N step" line (the pacing); "[PINDIAG] lever N adaptive: decoders<=2 share=0.9 ttft=120 gap_floor=8" once and base=/target=/adaptive=
# on every step line (the few-decoder policy); "[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier spill complete on cap_blocks=512 hard_max_blocks=4096 batch_blocks=512 warn_ms=1000" once and
# batches=/lifted= on every spill line (complete spills). Then, after the four boots of the pair (C1 L1 C2 L2): per user and turn the paired comparison of agent_turns (turn
# wall time, the time to the first token, the longest gap between two tokens of the stream, decode tokens a second; paired by index, never by unpaired medians) and of
# concurrent8_steady, each arm against the two controls and the control-to-control floor; the answers must be EQUAL turn for turn (the same checkpoint, greedy: a difference
# is a token a lever changed and is NO-GO). READ the arm with python3 scripts/ci/sched_report.py <arm container log> --second <control container log> reversed as needed (B
# over A): the engine builds of returning turns (kind=rebind) p50 / p90, the lean split A / B / C, the readbacks skipped, the backstop readings reused, prefill's share of
# the wall time while a prefill is pending, the rounds after each returning turn, the longest stretch without a decode round, the guard steps and the owed cap. Every figure
# prints "-" when no line is behind it. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window's W0 built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the
# models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. Duration (estimate): 50 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-all
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,agent_turns,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
